    "created_at": "2026-11-16T19:50:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T19:50:16Z",
    "body": "Measurement from #2238 (frame-cost probe, release build, fig8.step, 1600 x 1000 window, headless).\n\nState: 2D Adaptive operation, one welded face picked (the face with the most strips), Containment Outside, Boundary group open, area preview filled. Six still frames, no input.\n\n| Piece | ms per frame | Calls per frame |\n|---|---|---|\n| `scene/collect` (all of the scene) | 18.13 | 1 |\n| `scene/parts.boundary_preview` | 15.14 | 1 |\n| `scene/parts.boundary_preview.triangulate` | 15.12 | 1 |\n| UI pass (all) | 11.84 | 1 |\n\nThe same window without the preview (nothing selected) costs 1.47 ms for the scene. Debug build: the triangulation costs 177 ms per frame.\n\nCause: `world::collect_parts` (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/world.rs`) calls `region.triangles()` on the preview region of `boundary_viz::preview_fill` on each frame. The `boundary_draft::Preview` value is made again only when its key changes. Its triangulation is not kept, so each frame triangulates the same region again.\n\nFix direction (rule of #2238, `docs/decisions/2238-frame-cost-rule.md`): keep the triangles (or the GPU vertices) in the `Preview` value next to the region, and make them with the region. Pin it with a counter: a still frame triangulates zero times, and a changed key gives new triangles.\n\nIdle frames do not repaint (`state_redraw_delay` gives `None`), so the cost shows on each frame that input or a repaint starts.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
